max-visits: 1

= The Young Plan and the fall of the coalition

The Foreign Ministry under [? if foreign_minister_party = "Z": Heinrich Bruning ?][? if foreign_minister_party = "DVP": Gustav Stresemann ?] has agreed to the Young Plan, an agreement with the Western powers to reduce Germany's reparation payments and give us more fiscal autonomy. Simultaneously, France will agree to withdraw its military occupation from the Rhineland.

While this seems to be a positive development for the country, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> opposes the plan, claiming that any reparations are a form of national slavery. As such, they have exited the coalition with a vote of no confidence being called by the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span>. 

Whether the government shall fall is dependent on the vote.

- @no_matter
- @no_matter2
- @groko

@no_matter
title: The [+ chancellor +] government has lost the motion of no confidence. 
view-if: chancellor_party = "Z" or chancellor_party = "DVP"
subtitle: The anti-government parties have over 50% of the vote.
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; spd_in_government = 0; in_right_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; spd_toleration = 1; dnvp_relation -= 5; spd_relation += 3; dvp_left += 1/2; 

Unexpectedly, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> has decided to tolerate the minority government in order to secure passage of the Young Plan through the Reichstag. As such, the [+ chancellor +] cabinet will cling on until the vote on the Young Plan in March next year. 

@no_matter
title: The incumbent government has lost the motion of no confidence. 
view-if: chancellor_party = "DNVP"
subtitle: The anti-government parties have over 50% of the vote.
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; spd_in_government = 0; in_right_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; spd_toleration = 1; dnvp_relation -= 5; spd_relation += 3; dvp_left += 1/2; chancellor = "Luther"; chancellor_party = "I";

Unexpectedly, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> has decided to tolerate the minority government in order to secure passage of the Young Plan through the Reichstag. Furthermore, with the exit of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> from government, former Chancellor Hans Luther has been appointed to replace Gottfried Treviranus as Chancellor. As such, the Luther cabinet will cling on until the vote on the Young Plan in March next year. 

